<title>BAHRAIN: Bahrain allocates $119 mln for wage increases.</title>
<headline>Bahrain allocates $119 mln for wage increases.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bahrain is allocating 45 million dinars ($119.4 million) for wage increases in fiscal 1997 and 1998, the official Gulf News Agency reported on Sunday.</p>
<p>It said the Gulf Arab state's cabinet on Sunday approved the plan to allocate 20 million dinars to raise wages of government employees in 1997 and another 25 million dinars in 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;The cabinet agreed to prepare a draft law and submit it to the Emir Sheikh Isa bin Sulman al-Khalifa for ratification,&quot; the agency said.</p>
<p>The fiscal year in Bahrain starts in January.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.377 dinar)</p>
</text>
